{"questions":[{"question_id":"51wZzwh7cxI8Csq2","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"basics-of-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"acid-and-base-strength","type":"mcq","marks":1,"negMarks":0.25,"permalink":"among-the-following-compound-the-most-acidic-is-2011-marks-1-51wzzwh7cxi8csq2.htm","content":"Among the following compounds, the most acidic is","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"p-nitrophenol"},{"identifier":"B","content":"p-hydroxybenzoic acid"},{"identifier":"C","content":"o-hydroxybenzoic acid"},{"identifier":"D","content":"p-toluic acid"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>(i) The structures of the different organic compounds are as follows :</p>\n<p><strong>(A) p-Nitrophenol</strong></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbpr4/19eeb5df-b1e8-4bcf-b5ad-6e99989cecd8/d8d4f200-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbpr5.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 47 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbpr4/19eeb5df-b1e8-4bcf-b5ad-6e99989cecd8/d8d4f200-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbpr5.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04mbpr4/19eeb5df-b1e8-4bcf-b5ad-6e99989cecd8/d8d4f200-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbpr5.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbpr4/19eeb5df-b1e8-4bcf-b5ad-6e99989cecd8/d8d4f200-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbpr5.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbpr4/19eeb5df-b1e8-4bcf-b5ad-6e99989cecd8/d8d4f200-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbpr5.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbpr4/19eeb5df-b1e8-4bcf-b5ad-6e99989cecd8/d8d4f200-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbpr5.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbpr4/19eeb5df-b1e8-4bcf-b5ad-6e99989cecd8/d8d4f200-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbpr5.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p><strong>(B) p-Hydroxybenzoic Acid</strong></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbkt2/371b5d3c-346f-4248-8b82-8f28a515e3c1/d502db60-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbkt3.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 47 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbkt2/371b5d3c-346f-4248-8b82-8f28a515e3c1/d502db60-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbkt3.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04mbkt2/371b5d3c-346f-4248-8b82-8f28a515e3c1/d502db60-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbkt3.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbkt2/371b5d3c-346f-4248-8b82-8f28a515e3c1/d502db60-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbkt3.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbkt2/371b5d3c-346f-4248-8b82-8f28a515e3c1/d502db60-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbkt3.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbkt2/371b5d3c-346f-4248-8b82-8f28a515e3c1/d502db60-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbkt3.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbkt2/371b5d3c-346f-4248-8b82-8f28a515e3c1/d502db60-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbkt3.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p><strong>(C) o-Hydroxybenzoic Acid</strong></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbgbl/92990bd4-a7e5-4779-9ed6-b50b254f8919/d18bdd10-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbgbm.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 47 English Explanation 3\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbgbl/92990bd4-a7e5-4779-9ed6-b50b254f8919/d18bdd10-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbgbm.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04mbgbl/92990bd4-a7e5-4779-9ed6-b50b254f8919/d18bdd10-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbgbm.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbgbl/92990bd4-a7e5-4779-9ed6-b50b254f8919/d18bdd10-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbgbm.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbgbl/92990bd4-a7e5-4779-9ed6-b50b254f8919/d18bdd10-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbgbm.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbgbl/92990bd4-a7e5-4779-9ed6-b50b254f8919/d18bdd10-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbgbm.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbgbl/92990bd4-a7e5-4779-9ed6-b50b254f8919/d18bdd10-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbgbm.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p><strong>(D) p-Toluic Acid</strong></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbbzs/a03c8af1-2e99-4ee6-9fac-7673bd297483/ce33ff80-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbbzt.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 47 English Explanation 4\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbbzs/a03c8af1-2e99-4ee6-9fac-7673bd297483/ce33ff80-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbbzt.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04mbbzs/a03c8af1-2e99-4ee6-9fac-7673bd297483/ce33ff80-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbbzt.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbbzs/a03c8af1-2e99-4ee6-9fac-7673bd297483/ce33ff80-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbbzt.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbbzs/a03c8af1-2e99-4ee6-9fac-7673bd297483/ce33ff80-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbbzt.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04mbbzs/a03c8af1-2e99-4ee6-9fac-7673bd297483/ce33ff80-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbbzt.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04mbbzs/a03c8af1-2e99-4ee6-9fac-7673bd297483/ce33ff80-6027-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mbbzt.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>(ii) According to the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.093ex\" height=\"1.984ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1809.1 877\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(503,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(882,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> values, the order of acidity of these compounds is as follows :</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mfip1/19fb6190-286b-49e4-9835-c4ec26185e4c/429dc950-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mfip2.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 47 English Explanation 5\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04mfip1/19fb6190-286b-49e4-9835-c4ec26185e4c/429dc950-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mfip2.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04mfip1/19fb6190-286b-49e4-9835-c4ec26185e4c/429dc950-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mfip2.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mfip1/19fb6190-286b-49e4-9835-c4ec26185e4c/429dc950-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mfip2.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04mfip1/19fb6190-286b-49e4-9835-c4ec26185e4c/429dc950-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mfip2.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04mfip1/19fb6190-286b-49e4-9835-c4ec26185e4c/429dc950-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mfip2.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04mfip1/19fb6190-286b-49e4-9835-c4ec26185e4c/429dc950-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mfip2.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>(iii) Regardless of the substitution, phenols are generally less acidic than carboxylic acids. Therefore, p-nitrophenol is the least acidic, despite the presence of an electron-withdrawing nitro group.</p>\n<p>(iv) The \"ortho effect,\" i.e., the presence of an electron-withdrawing or releasing substituent at the ortho position relative to the carboxylic acid group, increases the acidity of substituted benzoic acids.</p>\n<p>Therefore, o-hydroxybenzoic acid is more acidic than p-hydroxybenzoic acid.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mhixj/2f1b0fa4-48c5-4504-983a-95f19d93d959/7a6ac270-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mhixk.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 47 English Explanation 6\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04mhixj/2f1b0fa4-48c5-4504-983a-95f19d93d959/7a6ac270-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mhixk.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04mhixj/2f1b0fa4-48c5-4504-983a-95f19d93d959/7a6ac270-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mhixk.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mhixj/2f1b0fa4-48c5-4504-983a-95f19d93d959/7a6ac270-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mhixk.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04mhixj/2f1b0fa4-48c5-4504-983a-95f19d93d959/7a6ac270-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mhixk.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04mhixj/2f1b0fa4-48c5-4504-983a-95f19d93d959/7a6ac270-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mhixk.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04mhixj/2f1b0fa4-48c5-4504-983a-95f19d93d959/7a6ac270-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mhixk.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>(v) The presence of an -OH group at the para position decreases the acidity of carboxylic acids due to its electron-donating nature (via the positive mesomeric effect, +M). This effect is stronger compared to the electron-donating nature of a methyl group via the positive inductive effect (+I) or hyperconjugative effect (+H).</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mk1qs/afe4afe6-3e81-4147-a647-1dd8ffcaba5f/c0914940-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mk1qt.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 47 English Explanation 7\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04mk1qs/afe4afe6-3e81-4147-a647-1dd8ffcaba5f/c0914940-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mk1qt.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04mk1qs/afe4afe6-3e81-4147-a647-1dd8ffcaba5f/c0914940-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mk1qt.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04mk1qs/afe4afe6-3e81-4147-a647-1dd8ffcaba5f/c0914940-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mk1qt.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04mk1qs/afe4afe6-3e81-4147-a647-1dd8ffcaba5f/c0914940-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mk1qt.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04mk1qs/afe4afe6-3e81-4147-a647-1dd8ffcaba5f/c0914940-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mk1qt.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04mk1qs/afe4afe6-3e81-4147-a647-1dd8ffcaba5f/c0914940-6028-11ef-a1c9-9b299e7750eb/file-jaoe38c1m04mk1qt.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Hence, the order of acidity of the compounds is :</p>\n\n<p></p><p>(C) o-Hydroxybenzoic Acid</p><p></p>\n<p></p><p>(D) p-Toluic Acid</p><p></p>\n<p></p><p>(B) p-Hydroxybenzoic Acid</p><p></p>\n<p></p><p>(A) p-Nitrophenol</p><p></p>\n\n<p>Option (C) has the lowest <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.093ex\" height=\"1.984ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1809.1 877\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(503,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(882,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> or the highest <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.355ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.955ex\" height=\"1.901ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1306.1 840.1\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(882,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>"}]}